iyama to walk through the famous Bamboo Grove and cross the Togetsukyo Bridge.\\n* Afternoon: Visit Kinkaku-ji (The Golden Pavilion).\\n* Evening: Take the evening bullet train back to Tokyo and get a good night's sleep.\\n\\nDay 5: Historic Tokyo & Departure\\n* Morning: Visit Senso-ji Temple in Asakusa and shop for cheap souvenirs along Nakamise Street.\\n* Afternoon: Pick up bags from the hostel and take the train to the airport.\\n* Fly back to Pune (via Mumbai/Delhi).\\n\\n---\\n\\nMust-Try Local Food (Budget-Friendly)\\n\\n* Onigiri: Rice balls wrapped in seaweed sold at convenience stores (under 150 Yen / 90 INR).\\n* Ramen: Warm, filling noodle bowls from ticket-machine ramen shops.\\n* Takoyaki: Crispy fried octopus balls found at street stalls.\\n* Gyudon: Beef or chicken rice bowls from cheap chains like Yoshinoya, Sukiya, or Matsuya.\\n* Matcha Soft Serve: Green tea ice cream sold near Kyoto temples.\\n\\n---\\n\\nStudent Budget Tips\\n\\n* Eat from Convenience Stores: \\\"Konbini\\\" like 7-Eleven, Lawson, and FamilyMart offer fresh, cheap meals (bento boxes, sandwiches, buns).\\n* Stay in Hostels or Capsule Hotels: Book dorm beds or capsule pods well in advance to save money.\\n* Use City Subway Passes: Buy a 24-hour or 48-hour Tokyo Subway ticket for unlimited, cheap travel.\\n* Carry a Water Bottle: Tap water in Japan is 100% safe to drink; refill at hostels and parks.\\n* Consider the Night Bus: To save on both travel and a night of hotel costs between Tokyo and Kyoto, take the Willer Express night bus instead of the bullet train.\\n* Duty-Free Shopping: Carry your student passport to get 10% tax exemption on shopping over 5,000 Yen.\"","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"travelItineraryFlow","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"92a7162702047368":{"spanId":"92a7162702047368","traceId":"2e8254f